Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: wait for session completion before reporting ended

Source MEEndOfPresentation means that no more input will arrive, not that
the transforms and sinks have consumed their remaining output. GE serializes
replay behind that drain. Reporting public ENDED early lets the client stop
pulling frames, or reset the frame sink for a seek, before the last demand
needed to forward the video end marker. The queued replay can then wait
forever for the old session to finish.

Use the existing MESessionEnded handler for the public ended state and loop
restart, as the original Proton-RTSP MediaEngine does. Keep the session's
drain barrier, marker generations, explicit seek-to-duration handling and
terminal-error handling unchanged. No delay, retry or timeout is introduced.

P12's immediate post-EOS MPEG A/V replay is the negative runtime control.
The same packets without audio pass, and continuing frame consumption for
300 ms before replay passes; neither diagnostic workaround is a product fix.
The new source must pass the original immediate-replay oracle before adoption.
---
diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -1251,17 +1251,6 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_session_events_Invoke(IMFAsyncCallback *iface,
             break;
         }
 
-        case MEEndOfPresentation:
-            EnterCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
-            /* Media Engine users may wait on ended state before replacing the
-             * source. Network streams can deliver source end-of-presentation
-             * before every renderer has drained enough to produce MESessionEnded. */
-            ended_event = media_engine_handle_ended(engine);
-            LeaveCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
-            if (ended_event)
-                IMFMediaEngineNotify_EventNotify(engine->callback, MF_MEDIA_ENGINE_EVENT_ENDED, 0, 0);
-            break;
-
         case MEEndOfPresentationSegment:
             EnterCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
             if (engine->presentation.frame_sink)
